    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the undisputed centerpiece of the lineup. With a score of 81.88, he is the only player in the \"Strong\" category, buoyed by a significant +16% park factor and an 8% boost from his prime spot in the #2 hole. Despite facing a respectable arm in Hancock, **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s aggressive approach against right-handed pitching provides the highest ceiling for stolen base production, a critical need for our 5x5 standing. Joining him as a priority start is **Jackson Merrill** (60.98), who capitalizes on the elevated xERA of Abbott to overcome a difficult platoon disadvantage, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (59.62), whose output is bolstered by wind-aided power potential and a positive platoon split against Webb.\n\nWhile the depth of our roster remains a strength, **Brayan Rocchio** serves as the most illustrative bench decision. He sat on the threshold of our activation criteria with a 38.06 score, falling just short of the 40.0 \"Floor\" requirement. While he offers some utility, the combination of a bottom-of-the-order assignment (#9) and a stagnant recent performance profile made him the logical cut to protect our remaining games-played allowance. Meanwhile, the team remains shorthanded with **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jordan Westburg** unavailable, forcing us to rely on high-efficiency matchups for role players like **Nasim Nunez** and **Coby Mayo** to bridge the gap.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in the matchup against Webb, who presents a high-floor challenge for **Curtis Mead**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** While the wind-out conditions at the stadium provide a marginal +5% boost to their scores, the elite efficiency of the opposing pitcher makes this a high-variance environment. Furthermore, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (56.35); his matchup against the low xERA of S\u00e1nchez has suppressed his score significantly. We are counting on his raw talent to outperform the projected headwinds of an elite opposing arm, but he remains a high-risk candidate if the pitch-tracking data suggests early-inning struggles.",
